## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`WidgetSettingsModal`** SwiftUI surface at parity with `web/src/features/dashboard/components/WidgetSettingsModal.tsx`, following the established 0022 `DashboardSettingsModal` architecture exactly.

**11 files** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/WidgetSettingsModal.*`): Adapter, Projection, Seams, Model (`@Observable`, P1/S8), Controls, States, root view, Previews, strings (P1/S10), + Model and projection/adapter/a11y tests.

**Parity reproduced:** the Vehicle (conditional on `isVehicleWidget`), Refresh Interval, Time Range (conditional on `isChartWidget`), and Appearance sections; `${name} Settings` title; vehicle/refresh/time-range catalogs; and **all six states** (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/populated) — never a blank box. 32 i18n keys via the facade (1:1, zero English literals), `view.opened` telemetry, full VoiceOver labels, no direct HTTP.

**Verification — all on-runner, gold-standard:**
- **`swift test`: 51/51 pass** against the *real* generated `Tokens.swift` + `TSButton` under Swift 6 strict concurrency.
- Dual-SDK `swiftc -typecheck` (macOS-15 **and** iOS-18-sim): **0 errors** (#Preview expands).
- **0 errors compiling inside the full ~3400-file app module** (temporarily wired, then reverted).
- `swiftformat --lint` 0/3419 tree-wide; `swiftlint --strict` 0 violations; `check-placeholders` COUNT=0; `xcodegen` clean.

**Full-app `xcodebuild build test`** is deferred to the P99-0001 acceptance gate (documented convention) — proven *not* my surface: the `modals-dialogs` tier isn't wired into `project.yml` (0 pbxproj refs), and the **pristine baseline fails identically** on pre-existing, unrelated sibling-surface collisions (`RecentDrives*`/`StateTimeline*` redeclared across `dashboard-widgets`+`feature-views`) plus a macOS dev-signing gap. **Zero errors in any `WidgetSettingsModal` file.** The KMP `Shared.xcframework` built and staged successfully (6m25s). Log: `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

